# Class -> Rust path glob (relative to the audited crate's `src`) map for scripts/audit-port.sh's
# per-class matching. Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are ignored. A class whose Rust home
# spans more than one file gets one map line per file — not one line with several space-separated
# globs, which the reader (`read -r cls path`) would only keep the first token of.
#
# This map is used against **two** crates, because Plan 5's port is split across them:
#
#   ./scripts/audit-port.sh drc crates/fr-board/src 'ClearanceViolation.java' scripts/audit-map/fr-drc.map
#   ./scripts/audit-port.sh drc crates/fr-drc/src   'DesignRulesChecker.java UnconnectedItems.java NetIncompletes.java AirLine.java' scripts/audit-map/fr-drc.map
#
# Task 6 adds a third, over a different Java package — the one class of `core/scoring` this plan
# ports (plan-5 ruling 5 leaves `BoardStatistics` itself to Plan 8, so it is deliberately absent
# from the glob and would report `UNMAPPED` if it were added):
#
#   ./scripts/audit-port.sh core/scoring crates/fr-drc/src 'BoardStatisticsClearanceViolations.java' scripts/audit-map/fr-drc.map
#
# Task 7 adds a fourth, over `io/kicad` — the whole package, not a glob: the four DRC report DTOs
# are ported into `report/mod.rs`, and the three KiCad board/session JSON classes are carried by
# the `// added in Plan 8:` roster at the foot of `lib.rs` (plan-5 ruling 13):
#
#   ./scripts/audit-port.sh io/kicad crates/fr-drc/src '*.java' scripts/audit-map/fr-drc.map
#
# The second glob widens as the crate fills up: Task 4 added `UnconnectedItems.java` (which
# declares no public methods, so it contributes no rows — the map line exists to name its Rust
# home), Task 5 added `NetIncompletes.java AirLine.java`, and as of Task 6 the plain `'*.java'`
# the plan asks for already resolves with no `MISSING` left — Task 7 runs both forms. A class
# whose mapped file does not exist yet reports every method `MISSING`, which is the point: the
# map records the obligation, the glob records how much of it is due.
#
# The paths below are relative to whichever `src` the invocation names, so the `ClearanceViolation`
# rows appear twice: once crate-relative (for the `fr-board` invocation) and once as `../../` (for
# the `fr-drc` one). Plan-5 ruling 9 puts that class in `fr-board`, because `Item.clearanceViolations`
# returns it and `fr-board` cannot depend on `fr-drc`; `audit-port.sh` resolves the `../` form fine
# (it globs `"$RS"/$map_path` and tests `-e`), so the plan's recorded fallback — a separate
# `fr-board.map` — was not needed. Of the two forms the plan offers for the row, this map uses
# **one line per Rust file**, which is what `crates/fr-dsn`'s map header prescribes and what keeps
# the audit scoped to the files that actually hold the port.

# --- drc/ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DesignRulesChecker       checker.rs
DesignRulesChecker       report/build.rs
ClearanceViolation       items/clearance_violation.rs
ClearanceViolation       board/clearance.rs
ClearanceViolation       ../../fr-board/src/items/clearance_violation.rs
ClearanceViolation       ../../fr-board/src/board/clearance.rs
NetIncompletes           net_incompletes.rs
AirLine                  airline.rs
UnconnectedItems         unconnected.rs

# --- io/kicad/ (Task 7, landed; Task 8 adds the serialiser) and core/scoring/ (Task 6) ----------
KiCadDrcReport           report/mod.rs
KiCadDrcViolation        report/mod.rs
KiCadDrcViolationItem    report/mod.rs
KiCadDrcPosition         report/mod.rs
# A DTO of four `@SerializedName` fields and no methods, so it contributes no method rows; the map
# line names its Rust home and keeps `from_violations` (the port of `BoardStatistics`' clearance
# block) inside the audited path.
BoardStatisticsClearanceViolations  statistics.rs
# The last three are matched only by the `// added in Plan 8:` roster at the foot of `lib.rs`
# (plan-5 ruling 13 keeps the KiCad board-JSON reader/writer out of this plan); Task 7 landed it,
# Task 11 folds it into the crate's `not ported:` roster.
KiCadJsonReader          lib.rs
KiCadJsonWriter          lib.rs
KiCadBoardJson           lib.rs
